  "body": "So I guess this has been discussed to death elsewhere, but naively putting on my web developer hat, something that's in a shadow tree is still \"in a document\". Maybe in English: the element is in the shadow tree, the shadow tree is in the document, therefore the element is in the document.\n\nHave we considered \"in a document's light DOM\" or similar?\n\nIt seems like regardless of what we do we're going to have to audit every use of \"in a document\" and figure out whether it should become \"in a document's light DOM\" or \"in a shadow-including document\".\n",
